I'm waiting for the sun, just to say...{fi}

00:00:07.940 --> 00:00:11.440
taiyou to machi awase

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:14.490
good morning to a brand new day.

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:14.490
ohayou BRAND NEW DAY

00:00:14.490 --> 00:00:17.700
Wearing a matching pair of shoelaces,

00:00:14.490 --> 00:00:17.700
osoroi no kutsu himo de

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:20.870
I will run out to my dear boyfriend.

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:20.870
kakedasou DEAR BOY FRIEND

00:00:20.870 --> 00:00:24.250
While I'm wearing my uniform,

00:00:20.870 --> 00:00:24.250
seifuku ni tsumekonda

00:00:24.250 --> 00:00:27.250
a premonition is calling out to me.

00:00:24.250 --> 00:00:27.250
yokan ga yobu no

00:00:27.250 --> 00:00:33.470
I wanted to line up with him in the prism.

00:00:27.250 --> 00:00:33.470
PURIZUMU ni kasanareba aitai watashi

00:00:33.470 --> 00:00:39.970
What does the flower bud think as it starts to grow?

00:00:33.470 --> 00:00:39.970
fukurami hajimeta tsubomi wa donna omoi

00:00:39.970 --> 00:00:46.730
A tail wind blew from the south, as if winking at me. {link, link}

00:00:39.970 --> 00:00:48.770
minami kara fuita oikaze ga UINKU shita

00:00:46.730 --> 00:00:53.030
{fad(210,0)}I want to spend more and more sparkling everydays with you.

00:00:46.730 --> 00:00:53.030
kirakira no mainichi wo kimi to motto atsumetai ne

00:00:53.030 --> 00:00:59.530
We'll find dramatic experiences to make today a better day...

00:00:53.030 --> 00:00:59.530
DORAMATIKU mitsumeatte kyou ga motto kagayaku

00:00:59.530 --> 00:01:05.960
...and find a more glittering new you.

00:00:59.530 --> 00:01:05.960
pikapika no atarashii kimi wo motto mitsuketai na

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:12.090
I want to show a top-class dramatic smile...

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:12.090
DORAMATIKU tobikiri no egao motto agetai

00:01:12.090 --> 00:01:18.510
...as I've been invited by the stage where love blooms.

00:01:12.090 --> 00:01:18.510
koi saku SUTEEJI ni sasowarete

00:01:18.510 --> 00:01:23.640
Ever-thrilling school days, Yeah Yeah!

00:01:18.510 --> 00:01:23.640
tokimeki SCHOOL DAYS YEAH-YEAH!

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:29.980
Original TV-Fansub: Ryoumi 
 Encode: Jumonji-Giri 
 Additional Work: ReDone-Subs

00:02:06.970 --> 00:02:10.860
It's a pleasant day today, isn't it, Seiyu?

00:02:17.700 --> 00:02:19.320
It's about time.

00:02:27.370 --> 00:02:31.380
Kazuki-chan, if you don't get up now, you'll be late.

00:02:34.270 --> 00:02:35.380
Okay...

00:02:43.440 --> 00:02:46.120
Are you awake, Kazuki?

00:02:50.840 --> 00:02:52.710
Kazuki!!

00:02:57.580 --> 00:02:59.510
Put me down!

00:03:01.950 --> 00:03:03.890
Please be quiet.

00:03:04.290 --> 00:03:08.350
Yuuji! You really are becoming more and more of a beast!

00:03:08.350 --> 00:03:11.330
Oh my, you failed again?

00:03:11.760 --> 00:03:14.910
And to think, I even unlocked the windows for you.

00:03:16.900 --> 00:03:20.490
Hey, Hatsune-san, help me~!

00:03:20.960 --> 00:03:23.050
One more chance.

00:03:30.480 --> 00:03:35.560
On note: Good morning, Neena.
 Be sure to eat everything! ~Mama {sorry, there's no way in hell me TSing this sign is going to make it look good. Another win for Ryoumi's AFX.}

00:03:34.140 --> 00:03:36.920
Nee-chan, are you amusing yourself at my expense again!? {Rw}

00:03:36.920 --> 00:03:40.530
Please help me, Hatsune~!

00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:42.460
Rotten scoundrel!

00:03:46.180 --> 00:03:49.910
What a lively house.

00:03:48.260 --> 00:03:52.000
Okay, let's stop this and have breakfast.

00:03:52.430 --> 00:03:54.560
Ah, Marie-chan!

00:03:55.800 --> 00:03:58.710
So, that's Marie-chan's house.

00:03:59.460 --> 00:04:04.470
Nyaa~haha

00:03:59.460 --> 00:04:04.470
Living 4

00:04:12.680 --> 00:04:14.310
Oh my.

00:04:16.100 --> 00:04:17.930
Oh what, a cat?

00:04:17.930 --> 00:04:19.780
What's so bad about the cat?

00:04:41.160 --> 00:04:42.640
Excuse me.

00:04:42.640 --> 00:04:44.810
What's wrong, Marie-chan?

00:04:50.970 --> 00:04:55.690
Hi! Everyone in Marie-chan's <i>family,</i>

00:04:55.690 --> 00:04:57.650
<i>good morning!</i>

00:04:57.650 --> 00:04:59.280
M-Morning...

00:04:59.280 --> 00:05:01.630
You're in middle school, right?

00:05:00.920 --> 00:05:06.220
Yessiree, and I've become Marie-chan's best friend since yesterday.

00:05:06.220 --> 00:05:07.910
My name is be Isokawa Neena.

00:05:08.220 --> 00:05:09.680
"Is be"?

00:05:09.680 --> 00:05:11.370
Marie's best friend?

00:05:13.870 --> 00:05:16.460
Marie-chan, good morning.

00:05:18.910 --> 00:05:24.420
I'm a little bit envious. Can I have
 the privilege of accompanying you all?

00:05:25.290 --> 00:05:29.390
Please be our guest. Welcome, Neena-chan.

00:05:29.390 --> 00:05:34.300
Thank you, Onee-sama. 
From this day on, I'm part of your family.

00:05:34.300 --> 00:05:36.300
Yoroshiku, please...

00:05:36.860 --> 00:05:38.330
Same here.

00:05:40.480 --> 00:05:42.410
Marie-chan!

00:05:42.920 --> 00:05:45.740
Allow me to explain,
 in case you didn't know.

00:05:46.050 --> 00:05:51.760
Due to current circumstances, 
we are eating at our neighbors' house,

00:05:51.760 --> 00:05:55.590
and are indebted to Kazuki-san and Hatsune-oneesama.

00:05:55.590 --> 00:05:58.530
We are not living together at all.

00:06:01.180 --> 00:06:05.970
You're so pretty, Marie-chan!
I want to eat you up.

00:06:05.970 --> 00:06:08.070
I'll be excusing myself here.

00:06:10.290 --> 00:06:12.930
Marie-chan, wait up.

00:06:14.170 --> 00:06:19.010
Do you have class chores today? 
 If so, Neena can lend you a hand!

00:06:20.640 --> 00:06:24.030
Oh, I won't lose in a race.

00:06:24.030 --> 00:06:27.820
DASH GO! LET'S GO! FIGHT!

00:06:27.820 --> 00:06:29.110
DASH GO! LET'S GO! FIGHT!

00:06:28.510 --> 00:06:31.360
Neena-chan sure is an "interesting" girl.

00:06:31.360 --> 00:06:34.270
She's the type that Marie hates the most.

00:06:34.270 --> 00:06:37.640
She just can't deal with persistent,
 meddlesome people.

00:06:37.640 --> 00:06:40.710
And if you want an example... here it is!

00:06:54.380 --> 00:06:55.730
Wait up.

00:06:55.730 --> 00:07:00.600
My butt is ruined... Ruined, I say...

00:07:04.800 --> 00:07:06.940
Hey, hey, hey, Marie-chan!

00:07:07.520 --> 00:07:10.930
Would you like your salmon roe salted or unsalted?

00:07:13.300 --> 00:07:14.370
Salted.

00:07:15.150 --> 00:07:17.830
Wait up, Marie-chan!

00:07:21.450 --> 00:07:26.610
Did you know? The jam and croquet breads sold at the cafeteria here are great!

00:07:21.460 --> 00:07:26.610
Note: Croquet bread = fried bread with minced meat and vegetables inside.

00:07:26.610 --> 00:07:31.090
Every type of bread gets 
sold out during lunch time.

00:07:31.100 --> 00:07:34.600
Many people got concerned,
 and more was requested...

00:07:36.090 --> 00:07:38.600
Hey, hey, hey, Marie-chan!

00:07:39.350 --> 00:07:43.090
Would you like a vacuum cleaner or an electric fan?

00:07:44.470 --> 00:07:45.810
A vacuum cleaner.

00:07:45.810 --> 00:07:48.470
Wa, wait up, Marie-chan.

00:07:53.420 --> 00:07:56.210
If you ever feel sleepy during class,

00:07:56.210 --> 00:07:57.990
the infirmary we just passed has
 two beds with really soft mattresses.

00:07:57.990 --> 00:08:02.000
the infirmary we just passed has
 two beds with really soft mattresses.

00:08:02.000 --> 00:08:06.220
And if the school nurse is in a good mood,
 she'll sing you a lullaby.

00:08:08.050 --> 00:08:12.470
<i>The first time I met Isokawa-san was yesterday.</i>

00:08:12.880 --> 00:08:17.790
<i>My impression of her as a kind and gentle classmate vanished in a mere thirty seconds.</i>

00:08:17.790 --> 00:08:20.770
<i>That was the beginning of a nightmare.</i>

00:08:22.300 --> 00:08:24.460
I'm Isokawa Neena.

00:08:24.460 --> 00:08:26.560
You can call me Neena.

00:08:27.930 --> 00:08:29.020
Hello.

00:08:29.310 --> 00:08:31.030
Wanna look at the textbook?

00:08:32.070 --> 00:08:33.530
Thank you very much.

00:08:33.990 --> 00:08:37.570
Wanna read some manga?
 I have an album too. {Ryomi: "comics" ~ one of the rare things I'll de-localize}

00:08:38.360 --> 00:08:41.450
My mom is American, 
and my daddy is Japanese.

00:08:41.450 --> 00:08:43.810
That makes Neena a half. {::trollface::}

00:08:44.660 --> 00:08:46.420
Hey, hey...

00:08:46.420 --> 00:08:48.680
Marie-chan, Marie-chan.

00:08:48.680 --> 00:08:52.880
<i>Would you like</i> cutting your nails
 short or long?

00:08:54.050 --> 00:08:55.380
Short.

00:08:56.920 --> 00:08:59.350
Wa, wait up, Marie-chan.

00:08:59.920 --> 00:09:02.960
If you want to use the restroom, 
 I recommend the one on the third floor. {rc}

00:09:02.960 --> 00:09:05.650
They recently added a bidet to it.

00:09:05.650 --> 00:09:07.810
Neena will take you there.

00:09:07.810 --> 00:09:08.650
No, thanks.

00:09:15.490 --> 00:09:19.950
This pool is used by the middle- and high-schoolers.

00:09:21.910 --> 00:09:25.870
Wow, amazing! Are we going flower-viewing today?

00:09:25.870 --> 00:09:29.840
Onee-chan, just how many people did you expect to be eating this?

00:09:31.540 --> 00:09:33.570
Here's your lunch.

00:09:33.570 --> 00:09:36.300
If there's too much,
 just share some with Yuuji-kun.

00:09:36.300 --> 00:09:38.580
There's no way I can finish this.

00:09:38.580 --> 00:09:41.750
But <i>I</i> can! And I will!

00:09:42.180 --> 00:09:44.160
What's wrong, Kazuki?

00:09:44.160 --> 00:09:46.110
Wait 'till Chihaya gets here.

00:09:46.800 --> 00:09:49.990
More importantly,
 have you behaved yourself?

00:09:49.990 --> 00:09:54.490
Don't tell me you've been creeping out
 all the girls in your class.

00:09:54.990 --> 00:09:58.160
You don't have to be all 
clean-cut like yesterday.

00:09:59.730 --> 00:10:01.250
YES!

00:10:01.250 --> 00:10:04.040
But at least don't go molesting anybody. 
That's all I ask.

00:10:04.040 --> 00:10:06.000
But at least don't go molesting anybody. 
That's all I ask.

00:10:06.530 --> 00:10:08.460
Yeah, about that...

00:10:08.460 --> 00:10:11.340
What? You mean you did "something"?

00:10:12.330 --> 00:10:14.760
I got tired of acting proper,

00:10:15.100 --> 00:10:17.900
so I greeted them
 as my real self today.

00:10:19.810 --> 00:10:21.390
GOOD MORNING, everybody!

00:10:24.020 --> 00:10:25.110
Who is that?

00:10:25.110 --> 00:10:26.930
He looks familiar.

00:10:27.350 --> 00:10:28.610
Is he your friend?

00:10:28.610 --> 00:10:29.800
Don't know him.

00:10:29.800 --> 00:10:32.310
Another new transfer student?

00:10:36.610 --> 00:10:39.670
Kazuki, your sister is such a good cook.

00:10:39.670 --> 00:10:41.750
When did you get here, Chihaya?

00:10:41.750 --> 00:10:45.370
I finally got them to understand that I was Kagura,{Ryo: After getting Kagura to explain to everyone, // wrong on so many levels}

00:10:45.750 --> 00:10:50.690
but the girls didn't want to have anything to do with me...

00:10:50.690 --> 00:10:54.230
There, there. Did they hurt you, little boy?

00:10:54.230 --> 00:10:57.260
I'd be glad to console you,
 if you think I can help.

00:11:00.210 --> 00:11:04.020
Ouch... Ouch... Ouch...

00:11:00.750 --> 00:11:04.140
Is this how you show your appreciation?!

00:11:05.240 --> 00:11:10.390
Then my only option is to get aggressive and go on the attack like I did in middle school!

00:11:10.390 --> 00:11:13.880
You'd better quit while you're ahead, before they hate you for real.

00:11:15.430 --> 00:11:20.130
But you'll still accept me,
won't you, Kazuki??

00:11:20.130 --> 00:11:22.240
I sure don't accept THIS!

00:11:22.660 --> 00:11:23.950
Eliminating.

00:11:30.240 --> 00:11:33.630
This courtyard is also shared by the middle- and high-schoolers.

00:11:33.630 --> 00:11:36.620
Sometimes, squirrels 
show up here during lunchtime.

00:11:36.620 --> 00:11:39.340
And if you don't share your food with them,
 they'll throw nuts at you.

00:11:40.370 --> 00:11:43.550
So, that's the legendary Neena-chan?

00:11:44.920 --> 00:11:47.010
What a lively child.

00:12:45.490 --> 00:12:47.740
<i>Please do not come near me.</i>

00:12:52.340 --> 00:12:54.160
<i>I can't get through them this way.</i>

00:12:54.910 --> 00:12:57.080
Marie-chan!

00:12:59.040 --> 00:13:00.250
Isokawa-san?

00:13:01.500 --> 00:13:04.040
<i>My best friend,</i> Marie-chan.

00:13:04.040 --> 00:13:06.720
I got worried 'cause I lost sight of you.

00:13:08.920 --> 00:13:10.680
<i>My natural enemies have doubled.</i>

00:13:13.590 --> 00:13:16.650
Oh? What's wrong, Marie-chan?

00:13:21.850 --> 00:13:23.760
Marie-chan?

00:13:23.760 --> 00:13:25.570
I'm at my limit.

00:13:28.060 --> 00:13:29.990
Oh yeah, I've still got leftovers.

00:13:34.240 --> 00:13:38.340
Let's see, where was that again...? Here?

00:13:39.620 --> 00:13:43.920
<i>Sorry,</i> I ate it all during my lunch break.

00:13:47.920 --> 00:13:49.680
I said "sorry."

00:13:56.220 --> 00:13:59.560
But... You're not gonna touch Marie-chan!

00:13:59.870 --> 00:14:01.480
<i>Isokawa-san.</i>

00:14:02.430 --> 00:14:03.590
Marie!

00:14:05.230 --> 00:14:07.740
Kazuki! Do we have leftovers from lunch?

00:14:07.740 --> 00:14:09.990
Yeah, there's some, but...

00:14:13.950 --> 00:14:15.660
Thank you.

00:14:16.230 --> 00:14:19.590
Here, have some fishpaste.

00:14:26.090 --> 00:14:27.390
They left.

00:14:28.770 --> 00:14:30.970
It's all right now.

00:14:37.380 --> 00:14:38.940
That's not like you.

00:14:42.560 --> 00:14:43.820
Marie-chan?

00:14:43.820 --> 00:14:45.280
Let her go.

00:14:48.140 --> 00:14:50.950
Mare-chan hates cats?

00:14:50.950 --> 00:14:52.050
Yeah.

00:14:52.340 --> 00:14:57.000
She doesn't like people
 who cling to her, either.

00:14:57.000 --> 00:14:59.680
Socially inept people like Marie...

00:14:59.680 --> 00:15:04.190
...should feel grateful that 
friends would come to their rescue.

00:15:04.190 --> 00:15:05.500
Yuuji!

00:15:08.360 --> 00:15:10.760
Is that so?

00:15:10.760 --> 00:15:14.520
And I was hoping I could be friends with Marie-chan.

00:15:14.520 --> 00:15:16.830
Oh no, please forget what I said.

00:15:16.830 --> 00:15:20.480
I was joking, it's all a joke, okay?

00:15:21.160 --> 00:15:24.030
Geez... What is he saying?

00:15:24.030 --> 00:15:27.410
Oh yeah, why don't you come to our house for dinner tonight?

00:15:41.200 --> 00:15:42.780
It's time to eat!

00:15:54.040 --> 00:15:55.390
Isokawa-san.

00:15:56.300 --> 00:15:59.140
Marie-chan, thanks for having me over.

00:16:02.050 --> 00:16:05.560
Neena-chan said that this is her first time making gyoza.

00:16:06.140 --> 00:16:09.670
Marie-chan, you come over here 
and help out too.

00:16:09.670 --> 00:16:10.490
Okay.

00:16:13.520 --> 00:16:15.500
Excuse me.

00:16:17.570 --> 00:16:21.130
Things sure seem awkward between them.

00:16:25.560 --> 00:16:29.380
S-Sorry! You can go first, Marie-chan.

00:16:29.380 --> 00:16:32.300
Will those two be all right?

00:16:32.300 --> 00:16:37.020
Well, whatever will be, will be.
We'll leave the gyoza to you two.

00:16:42.310 --> 00:16:50.100
Gyoza, meat buns, mabodofu, 
and Pitan are my favorite Chinese foods!

00:16:42.310 --> 00:16:50.100
Mabodofu: Szechuan-style bean curd with spicy meat sauce.
 Pitan: Chinese-style preserved duck egg, AKA 1000-year-old egg.

00:16:50.100 --> 00:16:52.150
Eh? Me too.

00:16:52.570 --> 00:16:54.610
You too, Marie-chan?

00:16:55.970 --> 00:16:58.130
That was a mistake just now.

00:16:58.130 --> 00:17:02.870
Actually, I hate gyoza, meatbuns,
 Mabodofu, and Pitan.

00:17:06.640 --> 00:17:10.710
The gyoza you made really are cute.

00:17:14.890 --> 00:17:16.620
Soft and fluffy...

00:17:16.620 --> 00:17:18.550
Mama told me...

00:17:18.550 --> 00:17:24.060
Cooking comes from the heart, and it's important for us to put our feelings into it.

00:17:24.060 --> 00:17:26.700
I hope this tastes good...

00:17:35.640 --> 00:17:37.040
Thank you for waiting.

00:17:39.060 --> 00:17:42.540
Sure is tasty over here...!

00:17:43.030 --> 00:17:47.250
Hatsune-kun, would you mind 
extending that slit upwards a bit?

00:17:52.040 --> 00:17:55.220
Never mind... I'm really hungry.

00:17:55.680 --> 00:17:58.180
Let's eat!

00:18:03.890 --> 00:18:06.640
Who made this gyoza?

00:18:07.120 --> 00:18:13.150
Neena did the best she could, but it seems like
 it's no match for Marie-chan's.

00:18:13.290 --> 00:18:15.110
<i>Yuuji!</i>

00:18:23.400 --> 00:18:25.290
But, it does taste good.

00:18:26.700 --> 00:18:29.040
Marie-chan, thank you.

00:18:29.680 --> 00:18:30.970
It's nothing.

00:18:31.950 --> 00:18:34.000
It is quite delicious.

00:18:35.200 --> 00:18:36.460
<i>I see.</i>

00:18:36.460 --> 00:18:39.300
And so, who made these lovely gyoza?

00:18:39.300 --> 00:18:40.970
That would be me.

00:18:43.920 --> 00:18:45.590
Yummy, aren't they?

00:18:45.590 --> 00:18:49.980
How could you use the same good ingredients and get such shitty results!?

00:18:50.580 --> 00:18:55.710
I added sour cream, natto, 
and strawberry jam as hidden flavors...

00:18:50.580 --> 00:18:55.710
Natto = fermented soybeans

00:18:55.160 --> 00:18:56.600
Don't add those!

00:18:56.600 --> 00:18:58.100
This is fun.

00:18:58.560 --> 00:19:01.440
Papa comes home late because of his job.

00:19:01.440 --> 00:19:04.080
So Neena always eats alone.

00:19:04.080 --> 00:19:09.170
But today, I'm very happy because 
I get to eat dinner with Marie-chan.

00:19:11.370 --> 00:19:13.090
One question.

00:19:13.090 --> 00:19:16.460
Why do you like Marie-chan?
 She's socially incompetent.

00:19:16.460 --> 00:19:19.420
Because, she looks exactly like Rakkun. {Racoon -obvious enough?}

00:19:19.730 --> 00:19:21.310
Rakkun?

00:19:19.730 --> 00:19:21.310
Rakkun?

00:19:22.880 --> 00:19:24.440
A stuffed animal?

00:19:24.440 --> 00:19:27.520
It seems that Rakkun really looks like Marie-chan.

00:19:27.520 --> 00:19:29.850
Never knew Marie had whiskers.

00:19:29.850 --> 00:19:33.310
Yes, I'd forgot to mention... 
oh wait, I <i>don't</i>  have any.

00:19:34.220 --> 00:19:38.100
I talk to Rakkun about everything that happens at school,

00:19:38.100 --> 00:19:41.080
which means that I told him a lot about you, Marie-chan.

00:19:41.080 --> 00:19:45.080
Rakkun sees you as being 
my number-one best friend.

00:19:47.370 --> 00:19:50.960
Your bear too, is most certainly cute, 
is she not?

00:19:51.660 --> 00:19:55.420
Thanks for protecting me 
from the cats back there.

00:19:56.490 --> 00:20:02.010
From now on, I suppose I can 
occasionally allow you to eat with us.

00:20:02.710 --> 00:20:03.830
Neena-san.

00:20:03.830 --> 00:20:07.950
Thank you, Marie-chan! Love ya~!

00:20:11.090 --> 00:20:12.880
Let's get along.

00:20:13.510 --> 00:20:15.230
Yes, let's.

00:20:15.470 --> 00:20:17.820
Marie-chan's big brother!

00:20:18.110 --> 00:20:21.080
It was because of you that we became true friends.

00:20:21.080 --> 00:20:23.640
Thank you very much for everything.

00:20:23.640 --> 00:20:26.990
No really, it's my pleasure.

00:20:26.990 --> 00:20:30.450
Too bad my little sister is so "little"...

00:20:30.450 --> 00:20:32.410
Just joking.

00:20:33.280 --> 00:20:35.170
You're despicable!

00:20:37.490 --> 00:20:38.590
Divine punishment.

00:20:44.750 --> 00:20:49.310
Neena's home is none too distant,
so worry not for her sake.

00:20:49.310 --> 00:20:50.650
It's around here?

00:20:50.650 --> 00:20:52.890
How close can it <i>be?</i>

00:20:52.890 --> 00:20:54.830
It lies right over yonder.

00:20:56.350 --> 00:20:57.570
"Yonder"?

00:20:58.180 --> 00:21:01.190
You mean it's on the top floor?

00:21:01.600 --> 00:21:02.900
YES!

00:21:04.480 --> 00:21:05.770
Very close.

00:21:09.320 --> 00:21:12.930
You can be a good brother, sometimes.

00:21:13.500 --> 00:21:16.240
We're the only siblings we have, after all.

00:21:17.380 --> 00:21:20.960
Did that score me some points? 
Have you fallen for me all over again?

00:21:21.790 --> 00:21:23.380
Not a chance!

00:21:23.680 --> 00:21:27.210
Oh, that's right, Kazuki!

00:21:27.210 --> 00:21:31.560
You should also wear a Chinese dress sometime!
 The high-slit kind.

00:21:31.560 --> 00:21:34.110
That's got nothing to do with Chinese dresses.

00:21:34.110 --> 00:21:37.560
Come on, what have you got to lose?

00:21:37.560 --> 00:21:40.740
I'll even help you change, too...

00:21:42.930 --> 00:21:45.490
Hey! Marie!

00:21:46.440 --> 00:21:49.120
It seems their routine still persists, Rakkun.

00:21:49.120 --> 00:21:52.250
Yoohoo, Neena, it's time to go to bed! {Ow, painful American accent}

00:21:52.250 --> 00:21:53.440
Okay!

00:21:54.740 --> 00:21:58.380
See you again at school tomorrow,
 Marie-chan.

00:22:06.220 --> 00:22:14.850
The first time we met was on that sunlit veranda... {fi, link}

00:22:06.220 --> 00:22:14.850
Hajimete deatta hidamari no BERANDA

00:22:14.850 --> 00:22:20.480
Do you remember that place? {video fi, fo}

00:22:14.850 --> 00:22:20.480
Oboeteru kono basho?

00:22:21.860 --> 00:22:31.700
Spending time together was like breathing air, {sc, sc}

00:22:21.860 --> 00:22:31.700
Maru de kuuki no you na futari no jikan

00:22:31.700 --> 00:22:38.500
and we didn't realize the beauty of that placid time. {fo? or sc}

00:22:31.700 --> 00:22:38.500
SUTEKI na koto kizukanai PLACID TIME

00:22:39.040 --> 00:22:46.010
Our feelings of missing each other gave birth to... {sc, link}

00:22:39.040 --> 00:22:46.010
Aitai kimochi kara umareta

00:22:46.010 --> 00:22:50.640
...the dreams that bloomed in our hearts, {link, link}

00:22:46.010 --> 00:22:50.640
Kokoro ni saku yume wo

00:22:50.640 --> 00:22:56.270
which became more and more colorful. {link, link}

00:22:50.640 --> 00:22:56.270
Nan domo irozuiteku dakara

00:22:56.270 --> 00:23:03.480
Will you let me stay by your side? {link, link}

00:22:56.270 --> 00:23:03.480
Anata no tonari ni isasete ne

00:23:03.480 --> 00:23:07.860
I hope our silhouettes... {link, link}

00:23:03.480 --> 00:23:07.860
Futatsu no SHIRUETTO

00:23:07.860 --> 00:23:19.750
...will continue this endless story tomorrow. {link, fo}

00:23:07.860 --> 00:23:19.750
Ashita mo tsuzuku to ii na endless story

00:23:24.960 --> 00:23:27.460
Next Episode

00:23:25.680 --> 00:23:29.610
Ah... Yuuji didn't use to be this perverted...

00:23:29.610 --> 00:23:33.470
I think he's just my type.
We've got things in common.

00:23:33.470 --> 00:23:33.940
Eh?

00:23:33.550 --> 00:23:40.110
I'll Break Up With Him!

00:23:33.940 --> 00:23:36.360
If you don't want him, I'll take him.

00:23:36.340 --> 00:23:39.460
Next time on Tonagura: I'll Break Up With Him!"
